<title>SWEDEN: Swedish unemployment falls to 8.3 pct in April.</title>
<headline>Swedish unemployment falls to 8.3 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's official unemployment fell to 8.3 percent in April from 8.4 percent in March, Statistics Sweden said on Thursday.</p>
<p> SWEDISH UNEMPLOYMENT	 April '97   March '97  April '96</p>
<p> Percent of workforce	 8.3	   8.4	  7.5</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	 350,000     355,000    318,000</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll of economists showed the market had expected an unemployment rate of 8.1 percent in April.</p>
<p>Sweden's Labour Market Board (Ams) released its unemployment data on May 7, saying unemployment was 7.5 percent in April this year, down from 8.0 percent in March.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
